ng to suggest a competitive race. Rick Brattin, the Republican nominee, has raised little and is fighting both heavy outside opposition spending and a lawsuit seeking to replace him on the ballot.\n\nExpert raters overwhelmingly place the seat in the Safe or Solid Democratic column, and prediction markets price Cleaver's chances near 90%. The main uncertainty is procedural rather than electoral: the GOP nominee dispute and any residual map litigation could reshape the race, but the fundamentals point to a comfortable Cleaver win.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9884, "margin": 16.87}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9807, "margin": 15.0}]}